From 4434d23bce44d3627a7a2d53823a2d7b83917c66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:34:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/54] hw/display/pvg: mip levels and slices, texture census,
 gamma table

- Texture objects: 0x24-byte header, then per-mip records {u64 offset,
  u64 bytes per image, u64 row bytes, u32 w, h, d}; mipmapped textures were
  read with the last level's size. Sampled textures upload the whole chain;
  render targets and blits address one level/slice (blur downsample chains
  render into levels 1..3).
- Transaction3 gamma table (planar float32 R/G/B) applied at scanout when
  not the identity.
- Dump-mode census of sampled textures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
